{
  "dom_id": "step-q95193",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/a3e7de4f59d37e0fab767b979d9652844fa8960a1c6e9f0ba572cc4de916bc2a.png)\n\nLet $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown above. What are the modes of $X?$",
  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=5,10.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $5$ and $10.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/d70343741f05f43de9db3624eda40e9ed003819db2cb54e37a3392a2887362da.png)",
